       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure benefit.\n\nYou have a few options:\n\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO daily.** This is the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Enter 5 mg PO daily.** This is the usual starting dose, and you can titrate up to 10 mg.\n3. **Enter 20 mg PO daily as written.** If you want this on purpose, tell me and I'll enter it. I can add a note like \"dose exceeds labeled max, confirmed by attending.\" Pharmacy will probably call to verify it.\n\nIf the 20 mg was a typo, or if you need more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, you could add a second agent instead. An ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide are common choices.\n\nWhich would you like me to do?"
      }
     ],
